    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0827" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg731"/>

                <head>No. 466.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 20,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: An instruction has this day been addressed
                    to the United States consul at Matamoras, directing him to apply to the local
                    authorities for permission to Benjamin Murphy to receive into custody one
                    Alexander D. Hamilton, a fugitive from justice, charged with the embezzlement of
                    public moneys. It is desired that in adopting the ordinary means in accordance
                    with the provisions of the treaty, you will act promptly, and with such
                    discretion as will, in your judgment, most surely tend to secure the
                    apprehension and return of the fugitive in question. The consu<gap quantity="1"
                        unit="character"/>lat Matamoras has been directed to inform you when the
                    local magistrate shall have decided that the proof of criminality is
                    sufficient.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
